<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vetkopers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th–15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vetkopers were one of two rival factions in late medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frisia">Frisia</a>, opposed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schieringers">Schieringers</a>. Their feud, which began in the 14th century and was linked to rivalries between chieftain families, monasteries and towns, divided Westergo, Oostergo and neighbouring lands, with the Vetkopers generally allied to the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/groningen">Groningen</a>. The conflict weakened Frisia until Albert of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> took control in 1498.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vetkopers.jpg" alt="Vetkopers" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julius Scholtz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Die_Westfriesen_tragen_Herzog_Albrecht_dem_Beherzten_im_Jahre_1498_die_Regentschaft_%C3%BCber_Westfriesland_an.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
